# The sdist's default file set (setuptools' add_defaults) picks up
# `tests/test*.py` by its optional glob, but NOT tests/conftest.py or
# tests/track5_helpers.py, which every one of those modules needs:
# conftest holds the sandbox fixtures that keep a run out of
# ~/.qualcoder_mcp and the real workspace, and track5_helpers holds the
# project builders and the REAL_WORKSPACE / REAL_STATE_HOME guards. The
# result was an sdist carrying a suite that cannot run, and whose test
# bodies are exactly the ones whose isolation is missing.
#
# Pruning rather than grafting: the whole suite would also need the
# shipped documents several modules read (CHANGELOG.md, PRIVACY.md and
# the rest) and the .github workflows the pin ledger scans, which is a
# much wider sdist for no gain. CONTRIBUTING documents the clone as the
# way to run the tests, and CI runs them from the checkout.
#
# MANIFEST.in directives are applied AFTER add_defaults, so this removes
# what the default glob added (fix round 4).
prune tests
